    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0303" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760D.61/1155: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grankulla</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsinki</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-21T17:00:00+02:00">February 21, 1940—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 22—1:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. My telegram 95, February 16.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d261-f1"/> Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs informed me today Finnish Government will not act for the
                    present on Hungarian suggestion for mediation of the conflict with Russia
                    because there seems to be no reason to suppose such action would be productive
                    of favorable result at Moscow at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
